    "Infinity isn't all that far away. Don't we have infinity in us too? The fact that we can think endlessly while we're living this life, life is finite but thought is infinite. That's how we should live. This piece can't be the answer to everything but let me try to work it out we all experience loneliness. If you say you've never felt it, that would be a lie. Whenever I was really desperately lonely, creating something became my answer. The sheer joy of making something that was mine. That is infinity. Infinity isn't so far away. Don't try to find the answer in infinity, find infinity in ourselves. Our lives are finite. People die someday. I'll die, my mom will, you will, even every single person in this world. Why not upload yourself to a computer or become a cyborg, you say? Then you might actually find yourself wanting to die. You might have enjoyed everything in the world that suits your tastes until life just gets boring. That's when you need creation all the more. I think making something of your own means being free to shape your own life without relying on outside sources. I got through countless lonely days by creating things too. That is infinity. We are already infinite. Eternal. We can make our own reality, we can make our own universe. So create. Anything is fine. Something you've only ever imagined, something you've always thought, man, I wish that existed. Whether it's only you who wants it or the whole world, make something. Pull that infinity out. Because that's what it means to be human, to be alive"
